Source: ethercat
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jeong Han Lee <jeonghan.lee@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-sequence-dkms, pkgconf, autoconf, automake, libtool
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://gitlab.com/etherlab.org/ethercat

Package: libethercat1
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libs
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: EtherCAT master userspace shared library
 Runtime shared library (libethercat, SONAME libethercat.so.1) of the
 IgH EtherCAT master for the Debian 13 EtherCAT environment.
 Applications that drive the EtherCAT master through the realtime
 application interface (ecrt.h) link against this library. The 1.0.0
 package set has no in-tree consumer; the library is delivered for site
 application authors. The ethercat command-line tool is self-contained
 and does not link it.

Package: libethercat-dev
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libdevel
Depends: libethercat1 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: EtherCAT master userspace library - development files
 Development files for libethercat: the ecrt.h and ectty.h headers, the
 .so linker symlink, the static archive, the pkg-config file, and the
 CMake package configuration. Install this to build applications against
 the IgH EtherCAT master realtime application interface.

Package: ethercat-tools
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: EtherCAT master command-line tool
 The ethercat command-line tool of the IgH EtherCAT master for the
 Debian 13 EtherCAT environment, with its bash completion. The tool is
 self-contained; the realtime application library is delivered
 separately by libethercat1, kernel modules by ethercat-dkms, and host
 integration (systemd, udev, configuration policy) by ethercat-host.

Package: ethercat-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, autoconf, automake, libtool, pkgconf
Description: EtherCAT master kernel modules (DKMS)
 DKMS source for the IgH EtherCAT master kernel modules (ec_master and
 the enabled device modules, generic profile). Kernel updates rebuild
 the modules against the target kernel via DKMS.

Package: ethercat-host
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ethercat-dkms, ethercat-tools
Description: EtherCAT master host integration
 Host integration for the IgH EtherCAT master on Debian 13: systemd
 service units, udev device-access rules with the ethercat system
 group, and the reference runtime configuration. The live
 /etc configuration is rendered by site provisioning; the service
 fails closed when no configuration is present.
